{%- comment -%}
  FIRST ACCESS V2: the signup form, which lives in a modal.

  THIS IS THE LIVE SIGNUP SURFACE. It renders on the COMING SOON homepage
  (templates/index.json) and at /pages/first-access, whose page record carries
  the template suffix "first-access-v2". The older V1 section survives only at
  /pages/first-access-v1 as an archived reference. So an edit here changes what
  every real visitor sees.

  ===========================================================================
  TWO SEPARATE, UNCHECKED MARKETING CONSENTS (owner decision 2026-11-18)
  ===========================================================================
  This form used to carry a HIDDEN field:

      <input type="hidden" name="contact[accepts_marketing]" value="true">

  Every signup was therefore recorded in Shopify as email-marketing SUBSCRIBED
  without the customer agreeing to anything, with no wording shown and so no
  wording to produce later. That is gone. Email consent is now a real checkbox
  bound to the SAME native field, so an unchecked box sends nothing at all and
  Shopify records no subscription.

  EMAIL CONSENT IS NATIVE; SMS CONSENT CANNOT BE. `contact[accepts_marketing]`
  is a field Shopify's own customer form understands, so the email opt-in needs
  no JavaScript and no app code to take effect. Shopify has no equivalent
  `contact[...]` field for SMS, so the SMS box is read by first-access-v2.js
  and sent to /apps/carat/first-access-phone, which records it through
  `customerSmsMarketingConsentUpdate`. Consent has to live where a STOP reply
  is honoured, and that is Shopify.

  A PHONE NUMBER IS STILL NOT CONSENT TO TEXT. The mobile field remains
  optional and carries no implication on its own. Ticking SMS requires a
  number (Shopify will not hold an SMS consent for an account with no phone),
  which the script enforces before submitting; typing a number while leaving
  the box unchecked captures the number and grants nothing.

  NEITHER BOX IS PRE-CHECKED, and neither is required to submit. Browsing and
  joining the list are both possible without agreeing to any marketing.

  NO EM DASH CHARACTERS, in markup or in comments. Owner rule for V2.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign t = 'templates.first_access_v2'
  # DISPLAY ORDER ONLY. These are launch priority, matching the feature
  # cards, with Loose Diamonds last. The stored tag values are the same six
  # handles they have always been, so nothing downstream changes: a customer
  # tagged `loose-diamonds` before this reorder and one tagged after it are
  # indistinguishable.
  assign interests = 'luxury-steals,group-buys,set-your-own-stone,custom-jewelry,engagement-rings,loose-diamonds' | split: ','
  assign interest_labels = 'templates.first_access.interests.luxury_steals,templates.first_access.interests.group_buys,templates.first_access.interests.set_your_own_stone,templates.first_access.interests.custom_jewelry,templates.first_access.interests.engagement_rings,templates.first_access.interests.loose_diamonds' | split: ','
-%}

<div class="fa2-form" data-fa2-signup>
  {%- form 'customer', id: form_id, class: 'fa2-form__el', novalidate: 'novalidate' -%}
    <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="first-access">

    {%- if form.posted_successfully? or posted -%}
      {% render 'first-access-v2-success' %}
    {%- else -%}
      <div class="fa2-fields fa2-fields--pair">
        <div class="fa2-field">
          <label class="fa2-label" for="{{ form_id }}-first-name">
            {{- 'templates.first_access.form.first_name_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <input
            id="{{ form_id }}-first-name"
            class="fa2-input"
            type="text"
            name="contact[first_name]"
            value="{{ form.first_name }}"
            placeholder="{{ 'templates.first_access.form.first_name_placeholder' | t }}"
            autocomplete="given-name"
            required
            aria-required="true"
          >
        </div>

        <div class="fa2-field">
          <label class="fa2-label" for="{{ form_id }}-last-name">
            {{- 'templates.first_access.form.last_name_label' | t -}}
          </label>
          <input
            id="{{ form_id }}-last-name"
            class="fa2-input"
            type="text"
            name="contact[last_name]"
            value="{{ form.last_name }}"
            placeholder="{{ 'templates.first_access.form.last_name_placeholder' | t }}"
            autocomplete="family-name"
            required
            aria-required="true"
          >
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fa2-field">
        <label class="fa2-label" for="{{ form_id }}-email">
          {{- 'templates.first_access.form.email_label' | t -}}
        </label>
        <input
          id="{{ form_id }}-email"
          class="fa2-input"
          type="email"
          name="contact[email]"
          value="{{ form.email }}"
          placeholder="{{ 'templates.first_access.form.email_placeholder' | t }}"
          autocomplete="email"
          autocorrect="off"
          autocapitalize="off"
          spellcheck="false"
          inputmode="email"
          required
          aria-required="true"
          {% if form.errors %}aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="{{ form_id }}-error"{% endif %}
        >
      </div>

      <div class="fa2-field">
        <label class="fa2-label" for="{{ form_id }}-phone">
          {{- 'templates.first_access.form.phone_label' | t -}}
        </label>
        <input
          id="{{ form_id }}-phone"
          class="fa2-input"
          type="tel"
          name="contact[phone]"
          placeholder="{{ 'templates.first_access.form.phone_placeholder' | t }}"
          autocomplete="tel"
          inputmode="tel"
        >
      </div>

      <fieldset class="fa2-interests">
        <legend class="fa2-label fa2-label--legend">
          {{- 'templates.first_access.form.interests_label' | t -}}
        </legend>
        <div class="fa2-chips">
          {%- for handle in interests -%}
            {%- assign label_key = interest_labels[forloop.index0] -%}
            <label class="fa2-chip">
              <input
                class="fa2-chip__input"
                type="checkbox"
                name="interests[]"
                value="{{ handle }}"
                data-fa2-interest
              >
              <span class="fa2-chip__face">{{ label_key | t }}</span>
            </label>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      {%- comment -%}
        THE TWO CONSENTS. Independent, unchecked, and each one named after the
        channel it authorises.

        EMAIL BINDS TO THE NATIVE FIELD. `contact[accepts_marketing]` is what
        Shopify's customer form reads, and an unchecked checkbox is omitted
        from the POST entirely by every browser, so "not ticked" reaches
        Shopify as "no consent" without any code deciding that.

        SMS BINDS TO NOTHING NATIVE, because Shopify has no SMS field on this
        form. `data-fa2-sms-consent` is read by first-access-v2.js and sent to
        the app proxy. It deliberately has NO `name` attribute: a named field
        would be posted to Shopify, which would ignore it, and a field that
        looks submitted but is not is how a consent gets quietly lost.

        NO `required` ON EITHER. Agreeing to marketing is not a condition of
        joining the list, let alone of browsing.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <fieldset class="fa2-consent">
        <legend class="visually-hidden">
          {{- 'templates.first_access.form.consent_legend' | t -}}
        </legend>

        <label class="fa2-consent__row" for="{{ form_id }}-email-consent">
          <input
            id="{{ form_id }}-email-consent"
            class="fa2-consent__box"
            type="checkbox"
            name="contact[accepts_marketing]"
            value="true"
            data-fa2-email-consent
          >
          <span class="fa2-consent__text">
            {{- 'templates.first_access.form.email_consent' | t -}}
          </span>
        </label>

        <label class="fa2-consent__row" for="{{ form_id }}-sms-consent">
          <input
            id="{{ form_id }}-sms-consent"
            class="fa2-consent__box"
            type="checkbox"
            data-fa2-sms-consent
          >
          <span class="fa2-consent__text">
            {{- 'templates.first_access.form.sms_consent' | t -}}
          </span>
        </label>

        {%- comment -%}
          THE POLICY LINKS SIT WITH THE CONSENTS, not in a page footer this
          modal does not have. Both open in a new tab so reading them cannot
          discard a half-filled form.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <p class="fa2-consent__legal">
          {{- 'templates.first_access.form.consent_legal_html' | t:
            privacy_url: '/policies/privacy-policy',
            terms_url: '/pages/terms-of-service'
          -}}
        </p>
      </fieldset>

      <button type="submit" class="fa2-btn fa2-btn--full" data-fa2-submit>
        {{- t | append: '.cta' | t -}}
      </button>

      <p
        class="fa2-error"
        id="{{ form_id }}-error"
        data-fa2-error
        role="alert"
        {% unless form.errors %}hidden{% endunless %}
      >
        {%- if form.errors -%}
          {{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }} {{ form.errors.messages.email }}
        {%- endif -%}
      </p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endform -%}
</div>
